{
  "about": "The attack matrix's written table of who may do what (WORKLIST P0.77), read by e2e/db/attack/attack.mjs. Each public table and view of the snapshot has an entry (a view's rows are its tables', so laid: false); a table with none fails the run by name. owner: the column naming whose row it is, {via, on} for a row owned through another, or house for a row no member owns. specimen: the row each owner holds, laid down as the house. In a row, {owner} is the owner's id, {username} their handle, {id} the specimen's own id and {id#2} a second one, {ref:table} the owner's specimen in that table, {ref:table@V} another owner's, {uid@V} another owner's id, {peer} and {peer2} two bystanders, {admin} the admin, {private} whether the owner is the private member, {later} a month from now, {new} an id no row has. variant: what a new row changes so it is not the specimen again (none: the specimen is taken away and laid again). acrossBlocks: the others rules hold for BK and BY too; otherwise no write reaches across a block. touch: the change an update tries; forbidden: changes no one may make to any row, their own included. read: who sees another's row (everyone, members, viewable, viewable-members, owner, owner+admin, none). self and others: who may insert, update and delete their own rows and another member's (all, unbanned, ranked, rank1, rank2, admin, none; ranked asks the rank alone, rank1 and rank2 the rank and good standing). hidesBlocked: a member never sees the rows of one they blocked or who blocked them. reach: a row of one's own whose set columns point at another owner's row, and who may add it for each owner. probes: one attack each, with the answer it must get. why: the rule in words.",
